{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"But now it began to rain terribly at night, all through Sunday and still this morning! What is this to become! Yet one must not give up hope. On Sunday morning I was glad that it was raining so hard—I had to rest once— but after dinner I had myself driven to the Augarten and to Nußdorf, despite the weather, on the way to which I saw a pear tree, as large as a pear tree can be, covered with blossoms; it has already borne fruit; I enclose here a little blossom, one for you, the other for those who themselves have blossomed from this land, as a sign of how greatly I recognize and value the excellence of such soil. — How the Augarten and Nußdorf are, I have provisionally gathered from this and found them very beautiful..."}}],"created":1795080438,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":168,"prompt_tokens":268,"total_tokens":436,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-xKwfmx7fSfob7LGyJ294B4xlFzJkDkAm","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":268,"prompt_ms":400.338,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.4937985074626867,"prompt_per_second":669.434327992846,"predicted_n":168,"predicted_ms":3989.817,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.891119760479043,"predicted_per_second":41.8565563282727}}